---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/rejoiner-vs-sendlane';
const title = 'Rejoiner vs Sendlane for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Sendlane has been acquired by Privy. Compare the product and support arrangement actually offered to your store with Rejoiner, including continuity for existing automations and the work each team will own.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How should a Shopify team choose between Rejoiner and Sendlane?",
    "answer": "Compare the current contract, support responsibilities and demonstrated refill workflow. Confirm the Sendlane continuation or onboarding path after its acquisition by Privy."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should pricing be compared at 15,000 contacts?",
    "answer": "Request current matched quotes including messages, implementation, support, overlap costs and replacement tools. No fixed contact-price estimate is established here."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better abandoned cart recovery?",
    "answer": "Request the same cancellation and purchase-handling demonstration. This page establishes no comparative recovery outcome or setup speed."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I migrate between them?",
    "answer": "Plan field mapping, permission and suppression transfer, flow ownership and rollback. Include reviews and forms if the current stack depends on them."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "It is a commerce email candidate to evaluate on actual event mapping and flows. It does not automatically replace support contracts, review widgets or SMS operations."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Sendlane SMS matter versus Rejoiner?",
    "answer": "Both currently position email and SMS offerings. Verify destinations, account access and the exact cross-channel refill and opt-out behavior instead of assuming a missing Rejoiner channel."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which handles winback and post-purchase better?",
    "answer": "Use the proposed gift, refund and refill cases to compare correct eligibility and operator effort. Do not assume lifecycle breadth from an old recovery-only label."
  },
  {
    "question": "What workflow test should decide the choice?",
    "answer": "Run the home-fragrance exercise and document the vendor-transition continuity answers before committing to a migration."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Rejoiner vs Sendlane</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Rejoiner vs Sendlane for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Sendlane has been acquired by Privy. Compare the product and support arrangement actually offered to your store with Rejoiner, including continuity for existing automations and the work each team will own.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Evaluating retention support during a vendor transition</h2>
        <p>Scope checked on November 24, 2026. This is a source-based comparison and proposed evaluation plan; no account tests or merchant results are claimed.</p>
        <h2>Current scope and ownership</h2>
        <p>Sendlane announces its acquisition by Privy and continues to present email, SMS, reviews and forms on its site. Rejoiner presents email and SMS retention with expert support. Do not infer that Sendlane has closed, that accounts automatically share Privy features or that Rejoiner stops at recovery email.</p>
        <h2>For an existing Sendlane merchant: establish continuity first</h2>
        <p>Before replacing a working stack, inventory forms, sender domains, SMS numbers, automations, review widgets, integrations and billing commitments. Ask your account contact which product will serve renewals, whether migration is required, and what notice and export process apply. The acquisition announcement alone does not resolve those account-specific questions.</p>
        <h2>Proposed exercise: home-fragrance refill and gift orders</h2>
        <p>Draft post-purchase care email for a candle and a later refill invitation. A gift order should receive appropriate care content without automatically enrolling the buyer into a personal-use refill assumption. A refund or replacement should change the next action. Demonstrate these cases in both products using the same order fields and non-sending drafts.</p>
        <h2>Make the service handoff concrete</h2>
        <p>List who designs the sequence, writes copy, maps gift information, approves the audience and handles exceptions. Rejoiner public materials emphasize expert partnership; Sendlane materials also emphasize support. Ask both for written deliverables and escalation routes. Support availability and managed implementation are different commitments.</p>
        <h2>Email and SMS should have separate promises</h2>
        <p>For the refill exercise, define which shoppers requested SMS and what content the permission covers. Decide whether a purchase cancels only the refill invitation or other promotions too. Demonstrate that rule across channels and check how an opt-out changes eligibility. Built-in channels do not prove every automation shares the intended suppression policy.</p>
        <h2>Budget the transition as well as the subscription</h2>
        <p>Use matched audience and message volumes, adding implementation, creative, domain work and any replacement for reviews or forms. Hypothetical transition example: five hours of flow mapping plus three of template work plus four of QA equals twelve hours. At an assumed $60/hour this is $720 of labor, excluding supplier fees and any overlap period.</p>
        <h2>Cut over by behavior, with rollback</h2>
        <p>Archive the current refill criteria and drafts before changes. Keep one sender responsible for each active cohort; disable the old equivalent before enabling the new one. Check an order, gift order, refund and repeat purchase against expected eligibility. A rollback needs current suppression and purchase records so it does not restart an old invitation after the shopper has already bought.</p>
        <h2>Decision</h2>
        <p>An existing Sendlane merchant should first compare the offered continuation path with a measured migration cost. A new buyer should obtain clear current onboarding and contract terms. Rejoiner is a relevant alternative when its agreed expert execution and demonstrated flows fit the work. Acquisition status alone neither forces migration nor proves continuity.</p>
        <h2>Where Sequenzy fits</h2>
        <p>Sequenzy lists Shopify customer, order and catalog sync and commerce email automations on its pricing page. Consider it when email is the job you need to replace. Demonstrate required trigger fields, stop conditions and channel handoffs before assuming it can reproduce this page’s exercise. Compare current quotes and implementation work; this page claims no automatic price or outcome advantage.</p>
        <h2>Primary references and limits</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://www.rejoiner.com/">www.rejoiner.com</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sendlane.com/">www.sendlane.com</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sendlane.com/blog/privy-acquires-sendlane">www.sendlane.com/blog/privy-acquires-sendlane</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">www.sequenzy.com/pricing</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Vendor pages establish advertised scope, not measured performance, account eligibility or contractual service. Confirm destination support and required features for the selected account. Have the actual messaging permissions and send settings reviewed for the regions you serve; product tooling is not a legal clearance.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/rejoiner-vs-klaviyo">Rejoiner vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-sendlane">Drip vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-sendlane">Postscript vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Email apps for fashion stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Rejoiner vs Sendlane FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
